// Marks through calls (plan d.3; A:1009, S 4.11): a source argument's mark reaches the
// result and a write through it is one report at the call; a read-only result's
// receiver; a store into a class that writes through its fields (rule (e)), at a statement,
// and at a call through the callee's own parameter, which rule (e) makes Write there
// (A:1359; a call's stores add no caller-side check, `D20-core-4`). Shapes: c.6
// (plan lines 974-975) receivers `&place [auto-borrow]` and `&*r [reborrow]`; c.7 (line
// 1010) the receiver's borrow last; c.8 (line 1028) `drop(x.f) [assign]` then the
// store.
// Heads (plan e): `book` hands out a writable reference, but `lib` is `const` (at the
// call, never also EN0614); `view` returns a read-only reference, so `push` cannot
// change it (EN0614, help: remove `readonly` from the return type of `view`).
